<title>POLAND: POLISH YR/YR CPI 17.3 PCT IN FEBRUARY VS 18.1 JAN.</title>
<headline>POLISH YR/YR CPI 17.3 PCT IN FEBRUARY VS 18.1 JAN.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish consumer prices rose 1.1</p>
<p>percent in February against a 2.9 percent rise in January,</p>
<p>bringing year-on-year inflation down to 17.3 percent, the</p>
<p>Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>CPI rose four percent in the January-February period,</p>
<p>compared with a five percent rise in the corresponding period</p>
<p>last year.</p>
<p> POLISH CONSUMER PRICES    FEB 97    JAN 97	 FEB 96</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)    1.1	 2.9	     1.5</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)	   17.3	18.1	    20.4</p>
<p> services m/m change	   1.9	 0.3	     1.8</p>
<p> services yr/yr change	20.7	19.5	    21.0</p>
<p> food prices m/m change	0.4	 2.4	     1.8</p>
<p> food prices yr/yr change   16.3	19.0	    17.0</p>
<p>NOTE - revised figures in brackets</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
